# oracle: fix external pf/array without a library caller (its forces, energy and virial stay zero): an LJ melt where half the atoms carry the fix (applied every 2 steps), its scalar, per-atom array and fix_modify energy/virial in the thermo output, then a minimization through min_post_force
# Measured with native LAMMPS: max relative error engine vs native thermo 7.0e-15, atoms 9.5e-14.
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all
units           lj
atom_style      atomic
lattice         fcc 0.8442
region          box block 0 4 0 4 0 4
create_box      1 box
create_atoms    1 box
mass            1 1.0
velocity        all create 3.0 87287 loop geom
pair_style      lj/cut 2.5
pair_coeff      1 1 1.0 1.0 2.5
region          half block 0 2 INF INF INF INF
group           half region half
fix             e half external pf/array 2
fix_modify      e energy yes virial yes
compute         fe all reduce sum f_e[1] f_e[2] f_e[3]
fix             1 all nve
thermo_style    custom step temp pe etotal press f_e c_fe[1] c_fe[2] c_fe[3]
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
thermo          10
run             50
unfix           1
minimize        0 0 20 40
